monitor.jl writes monitor.csv to the experiment's output folder every [output] monitor_hours (default 1;
0 = off): the net transport through the Atlantic and Pacific sides, the domain-mean η of the model and
of GLORYS, the change in η over the shelf and the deep ocean, a volume budget accumulated every time
step (through the open sides, across the surface, and the residual, which should be zero), the net
inflow implied by the change in volume, and where the fastest velocity is.

plotting/volume_budget.jl checks that the volume control does what it should (the budget closes and the
model's mean η follows GLORYS's); plotting/max_speed.jl shows where and when the fastest flow is, to
catch boundary or bottom jets early. Both read the config like the other plotting scripts.

Taken from fjp/nested (monitor.jl, plot_budget.jl, plot_max_speed.jl), without the diagnostics of the
volume-control approaches that were dropped (edge η offsets, Flather η inflow, pin correction) and the
gateway monitor, which the online transports of #41 replace.

